---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/paper.css';
const portfolios = [
  { id: 'news-guarded', number: '01', name: 'AI + news', model: 'TimesFM + JEV', description: 'Trades on price forecasts. Negative news can block a new buy.' },
  { id: 'price-only', number: '02', name: 'Price AI', model: 'TimesFM only', description: 'The same trading rules, without the news filter.' },
  { id: 'reference', number: '03', name: 'Buy & hold', model: 'Market reference', description: 'Buys BTC, ETH and SOL once, then holds. No AI decisions.' },
];
---
<Layout title="The live paper portfolio" description="Compare three $10,000 virtual portfolios. See what each strategy holds, how its value changes, and why it buys, sells or waits.">
  <div class="wrap paper-wrap" data-paper>
    <header class="paper-hero">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">THE LIVE PAPER PORTFOLIO</p><h1>Three strategies.<br />$10,000 each.</h1></div>
      <div class="paper-intro"><p>Each strategy gets <strong>$10,000 in virtual cash.</strong> Real market prices, simulated trades.</p><p>Do price forecasts, a news filter or a plain trend rule improve on buy &amp; hold? Follow every trade and every decision to wait.</p><a class="text-link" href="#how-it-works">How the experiment works</a></div>
    </header>
    <div class="paper-status"><div><span class="pill" data-status>Loading snapshot</span><p data-freshness role="status">Getting the latest portfolio values…</p></div><button class="paper-button secondary" data-refresh type="button">Refresh data</button></div>
    <p class="notice" data-error role="alert" hidden></p>
    <section class="experiment-picker" aria-labelledby="experiment-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE THE EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="experiment-title" data-experiment-title>Loading experiments…</h2><p data-experiment-note class="section-caption">Each experiment has its own start date and three separate virtual portfolios.</p></div>
      <label>Experiment <select data-run disabled aria-label="Choose an experiment"><option>Loading…</option></select></label>
      <p class="fine-print experiment-caveat">Compare the three portfolios within the selected experiment. Experiments started at different times; their total returns are not a like-for-like ranking. The original experiment continues alongside the new one.</p>
    </section>
    <noscript><p class="notice">The interactive portfolio needs JavaScript. You can still <a href="/api/paper">read the current public snapshot</a> and <a href="#how-it-works">learn how the experiment works</a>.</p></noscript>
    <div data-live hidden>
      <section id="compare" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
        <div class="paper-section-head"><div><h2 id="compare-title">Meet the portfolios.</h2><p class="section-caption">All three run automatically. Select a portfolio to inspect its decisions and holdings.</p></div><span class="fine-print" data-started></span></div>
        <div class="strategy-cards" role="group" aria-label="Choose a portfolio">
          {portfolios.map(p => <button type="button" class={`strategy-card ${p.id}`} data-portfolio={p.id} aria-pressed={p.id === 'news-guarded' ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls="portfolio-detail">
            <span class="strategy-top"><span class="strategy-number">{p.number}</span><span class="strategy-title">{p.name}</span><span class="series-sample" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
            <span class="strategy-model">{p.model}</span><span class="strategy-description">{p.description}</span>
            <span class="strategy-value" data-card-value>—</span><span class="strategy-return" data-card-return></span>
            <span class="strategy-bottom"><span data-card-state>Waiting for data</span><span class="strategy-choose" data-card-choice>Select portfolio</span></span>
          </button>)}
        </div>
        <div class="portfolio-shortcut"><span data-selection-copy>AI + news is selected.</span><a href="#portfolio-detail">Explore its decisions &amp; holdings</a></div>
      </section>
      <section class="paper-panel chart-panel" aria-labelledby="value-title">
        <div class="paper-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">PORTFOLIO PERFORMANCE</p><h2 id="value-title">What changed since the start?</h2></div><div class="chart-switch" role="group" aria-label="Chart display"><button type="button" data-chart-mode="all" aria-pressed="true">Compare all</button><button type="button" data-chart-mode="selected" aria-pressed="false">Selected portfolio</button></div></div>
        <p class="section-caption">Profit or loss in USD, after simulated trading costs. The zero line means your starting $10,000 is unchanged.</p>
        <div class="paper-legend" aria-label="Chart legend"><span class="news-guarded" data-legend="news-guarded"><i class="series-sample" aria-hidden="true"></i>01 · AI + news</span><span class="price-only" data-legend="price-only"><i class="series-sample" aria-hidden="true"></i>02 · Price AI</span><span class="reference" data-legend="reference"><i class="series-sample" aria-hidden="true"></i>03 · Buy & hold</span><span class="cash-legend"><i class="series-sample" aria-hidden="true"></i>Cash · $0 change</span></div>
        <div class="paper-chart-wrap"><svg data-equity-chart viewBox="0 0 960 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="equity-chart-title equity-chart-desc"><title id="equity-chart-title">Change in virtual portfolio value</title><desc id="equity-chart-desc">Profit or loss for the three portfolios relative to their own $10,000 start.</desc></svg></div>
        <p class="chart-explanation" data-chart-explanation></p>
        <div class="chart-foot"><span class="fine-print" data-chart-period></span><span class="fine-print">Scale adjusts to the observed changes.</span></div>
        <details class="chart-data"><summary>View exact values and comparison notes</summary><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Portfolio comparison"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Portfolio</th><th scope="col">Total value</th><th scope="col">Gain / loss</th><th scope="col">In crypto</th><th scope="col">Trades</th></tr></thead><tbody data-comparison></tbody></table></div><p class="fine-print">Each portfolio has its own $10,000 and the same start time. The cash baseline makes no trades. Exposure and execution times differ, so this comparison alone cannot prove a benefit from JEV. Up to 30 days of hourly observations are shown. Unreliable observations break the chart line.</p></details>
      </section>
      <section id="portfolio-detail" class="portfolio-detail news-guarded" aria-labelledby="detail-title">
        <div class="paper-section-head detail-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">SELECTED PORTFOLIO <span data-selected-number>01</span></p><h2 id="detail-title" data-selected-name>AI + news</h2><p class="section-caption" data-account-note></p></div><a class="text-link" href="#compare">Change portfolio</a></div>
        <nav class="detail-nav" aria-label="Portfolio sections"><a href="#latest-decision">Latest decisions</a><a href="#holdings">Holdings & trades</a><a href="#decision-history">Decision history</a></nav>
        <div class="paper-metrics">
          <article><span>Total value</span><strong data-equity>—</strong><small data-return></small></article>
          <article><span>Cash available</span><strong data-cash>—</strong><small data-exposure></small></article>
          <article><span>Completed trades</span><strong data-fills>—</strong><small data-trade-breakdown></small><small data-fees></small></article>
          <article><span>Largest fall from a peak</span><strong data-drawdown>—</strong><small data-brake></small></article>
        </div>
        <section class="latest-decisions" id="latest-decision" aria-labelledby="latest-title"><div class="paper-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY IT ACTED — OR WAITED</p><h3 id="latest-title">The latest decision for each coin.</h3></div><span class="fine-print">New decisions about once an hour</span></div><p data-latest-summary class="latest-summary" role="status"></p><div class="latest-grid" data-latest></div><p class="fine-print" data-latest-note>A forecast is an estimate. The entry threshold includes trading costs and an uncertainty allowance. Cash is a valid position when a signal is too weak.</p></section>
        <section class="paper-panel" id="holdings" aria-labelledby="holdings-title"><div class="paper-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHERE THE VIRTUAL MONEY IS</p><h3 id="holdings-title">Holdings & cash</h3></div><span class="fine-print" data-holdings-asof></span></div><div class="allocation-strip" data-allocation role="img" aria-label="Cash and crypto allocation"></div><div class="allocation-labels" data-allocation-labels></div><p data-holdings-empty class="empty-explanation" hidden></p><div class="table-scroll" data-holdings-table tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Virtual holdings"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Asset</th><th scope="col">Units held</th><th scope="col">Price now</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Share</th><th scope="col">Gain / loss*</th></tr></thead><tbody data-holdings></tbody></table></div><p class="fine-print" data-holdings-footnote>*Change in the value of held coins versus their purchase cost, including buy fees. Cash is shown above.</p></section>
        <section class="paper-panel" aria-labelledby="trade-title"><div class="paper-section-head"><div><h3 id="trade-title">Completed trades</h3><p class="section-caption">Actual simulated buys and sells for this portfolio.</p></div><span class="pill">Virtual money only</span></div><div data-trade-empty class="empty-explanation" hidden><strong>No trades completed yet.</strong><p data-trade-empty-note></p><a href="#latest-decision">See why it is waiting</a></div><ol class="trade-story" data-trade-story hidden aria-label="What this portfolio did, newest first"></ol><div class="table-scroll" data-trade-table tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Simulated trades"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Time · UTC</th><th scope="col">Trade</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">Units</th><th scope="col">Execution price</th><th scope="col">Trade value</th><th scope="col">Fee</th></tr></thead><tbody data-trades></tbody></table></div><p class="fine-print">Execution prices include order-book depth and 0.05% adverse slippage. A 0.10% fee is shown separately. These are simulation assumptions.</p></section>
        <section class="paper-audit" id="decision-history" aria-labelledby="audit-title"><div class="paper-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">EVERY DECISION LEAVES A RECORD</p><h3 id="audit-title">Decision history</h3></div><label>Show <select data-action><option value="all">All decisions</option><option value="trades">Buy / sell decisions</option><option value="blocked">Blocked decisions</option><option value="hold">Waiting / holding</option></select></label></div><p class="section-caption">Expand a row for the explanation. Technical evidence is available inside each decision.</p><div data-decisions></div><button class="paper-button secondary history-more" data-history-more type="button" hidden>Show more decisions</button><p class="fine-print" data-audit-note></p><div class="paper-export"><a class="text-link" data-download href="/api/paper" download="crypto-oracle-paper.json">Download public data</a><details class="journal-details"><summary>About this record</summary><p class="fine-print" data-journal></p></details></div></section>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="how-paper-works" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title"><p class="eyebrow">A QUICK GUIDE</p><h2 id="how-title">From market data to a virtual trade.</h2><p class="section-caption">The two AI portfolios follow these steps. Buy & hold makes one initial purchase attempt per coin, then keeps its positions. The trend experiment skips steps two and three: it reads completed daily closes instead of a forecast and uses no news.</p><ol class="paper-steps"><li><strong>Check the market</strong><p>Compare prices and available liquidity across Coinbase, Kraken and Binance. Unreliable data blocks new buys.</p></li><li><strong>Read the forecast</strong><p>TimesFM estimates prices 24 hours ahead. A buy needs enough potential gain to cover costs and uncertainty.</p></li><li><strong>Apply the news filter</strong><p>In AI + news, JEV checks recent headlines. A material negative event can veto a buy. Price AI skips this step.</p></li><li><strong>Trade within limits</strong><p>The simulator checks risk limits and records a buy, sell or wait decision. Every outcome stays in the journal.</p></li></ol><div class="experiment-facts"><p><strong>Every hour</strong><span>New trading decisions</span></p><p><strong>About every 15 minutes</strong><span>Values and public data update</span></p><p><strong>BTC · ETH · SOL</strong><span>Three coins, virtual USD accounting</span></p></div><p class="fine-print">This is an early technology experiment. Returns include assumed fees and slippage; they do not establish a durable trading advantage. JEV classifies headlines, not the truth of the market.</p></section>
    <section class="reading-content paper-rules" id="rules"><p class="eyebrow">FROZEN BEFORE THE FIRST TRADE</p><h2>The rules behind the numbers.</h2>
      <details open><summary>00 / Three experiments, separate histories</summary><p><strong>Trend filter (v3):</strong> no forecast, no news and no fitted number. At each completed daily close the rule counts how many of a coin’s 7-, 14-, 28- and 56-day returns are positive and wants 20% × that share in the coin; the rest is cash. It checks hourly, trades at most once per coin and UTC day, and only when current and wanted weights differ by more than five points in total. Two comparisons start with it: 20 / 20 / 20 / 40 rebalanced under the same five-point rule, and the same purchase held without rebalancing. There is no stop and no drawdown brake, because the published backtest had none. The rule came from that backtest; this run is its prospective test.</p><p><strong>Common start (v2):</strong> each portfolio receives a new virtual $10,000 and targets $2,000 per coin. All nine initial buys commit together against the same subsequent market observation, or all are cancelled. Costs and order allowances mean the filled weights are slightly below 20% per coin. A failed setup waits for a new hourly attempt at new prices. Market-data and execution checks always apply. Forecasts and news are recorded for context; their entry rules begin after this fixed setup.</p><p><strong>Cash start (v1):</strong> both AI portfolios begin entirely in cash and require a positive forecast to enter. Its reference buys once. This original run continues with its original rules and history. Nothing is backdated or reset. In both experiments, AI strategies use a six-hour interval for regular trades after each fill; stops and allocation reductions can act sooner.</p></details><details><summary>01 / A price signal with a separate news guard</summary><p>Both active strategies use the latest already-issued 24-hour TimesFM forecast. Its projected USDT price is converted with an observed USDT/USD quote and compared with the current Coinbase USD price. A buy needs an expected return greater than round-trip fees, slippage, spread and an uncertainty margin. The margin is the largest of 0.25%, 20% of trailing daily volatility, or 5% of the raw log interval width. These are fixed experimental rules, not calibrated probabilities.</p><p>The JEV variant can block a new buy when a recent headline is classified as negative and material, relevant to the asset, and related to security, regulation, a network or an exchange. Relevance and materiality must each score at least 0.70. Headlines are deduplicated by URL and cluster, and must have been observed and classified before the decision. JEV does not increase a forecast or order size. Missing annotations remain unknown; the small price-based experiment can still proceed.</p></details>
      <details><summary>02 / Plausibility before conviction</summary><p>New risk requires fresh books from Coinbase, Kraken and Binance, USD/USDT conversion within 1% of parity, agreement across converted prices within 1%, and a Coinbase spread no wider than 30 basis points. Maximum quote age is 45 seconds. The original 512-hour input artifact, its hash, completed hourly sequence, observation times and model revision are checked. No model score can override a failed data gate.</p><p>Risk-reducing sales still need a fresh Coinbase book and agreement with Kraken. A common price drop is not automatically a data error. If reliable marks disappear, the last marks are labelled stale and new risk is blocked.</p></details>
      <details><summary>03 / Small positions, explicit exits</summary><p>After the common initial allocation, each additional AI buy uses at most 5% of current equity, reduced when trailing daily volatility exceeds 3%. The original cash-start experiment applies this rule from its first AI buy. Total crypto exposure is capped at 60% and an asset at 25% when allocating. Regular trades in an asset are at least six hours apart. Risk reduction bypasses that cooldown.</p><p>A position can be sold after a 6% loss against its average cost, an allocation breach, or a sufficiently negative forecast. An 8% portfolio drawdown permanently pauses new buys in that strategy version. Existing positions can still be reduced. Gaps and unavailable quotes can increase losses; these rules do not guarantee a maximum loss.</p></details>
      <details><summary>04 / What a simulated fill means</summary><p>Orders execute only against a new book requested after the decision. The simulator walks visible bid or ask levels within 30 basis points of the best price, adds 0.05% adverse slippage and charges 0.10% per fill. These are simulation assumptions, not your actual Coinbase fee tier. Cash and allocation limits are checked again at execution.</p><p>Fills are all-or-none: insufficient depth cancels the order. Unfilled orders expire after 120 seconds and a restart never invents a fill at a past price. Execution is in USD pairs; there is no implicit USD=USDT trade and no real exchange order.</p></details>
      <details><summary>05 / An audit trail, not a performance promise</summary><p>Decisions are recorded hourly; valuations and public snapshots update on the server’s roughly 15-minute cycle. Deposits, observations, decisions, orders, fills, cancellations and valuations form an append-only journal. Its hash chain is checked on the server before export. That is an integrity check, not independent verification of market truth.</p><p>The snapshot includes recent decisions and trades, plus up to 30 days of hourly values. Raw books, full historical trails and model artifacts remain on the research server. No manual holdings, credentials or raw headline text are exported. The first 30 days test operation; they cannot prove a durable trading advantage.</p></details>
      <a class="text-link" href="/method/#confidence">How confidence and input quality differ ↗</a>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script is:inline src="/scripts/paper.js" defer></script>
</Layout>
